他表现得非常奇怪。

612
00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:58.440
She clearly knows something is up because he was moaning in his office, and Jan visited.
她显然知道有情况，因为他在办公室里呻吟过，而且简还来过。

613
00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:00.620
So Pam's like, what's going on, Michael?
所以潘就问，怎么了，迈克尔？

614
00:28:01.480 --> 00:28:04.460
Yeah, I have a fan catch from this moment.
对，我这里有个粉丝抓包环节。

615
00:28:04.740 --> 00:28:05.320
Okay.
好的。

616
00:28:05.840 --> 00:28:09.640
At 6 minutes, 21 seconds, Celeste Dimas says,
在6分21秒的时候，塞莱斯特·迪马斯说：

617
00:28:09.640 --> 00:28:15.120
If you freeze and look closely on that big board that's hanging by accounting,
如果你暂停并仔细看财务部旁边挂着的那块大白板，

618
00:28:15.540 --> 00:28:18.020
on Tuesday the 5th, it says,
在5号星期二的那天，上面写着：

619
00:28:18.780 --> 00:28:22.700
One of many Emmys, Steve, was robbed.
史蒂夫错失了本该属于他的众多艾美奖之一。

620
00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:26.720
Oh, that's a great fan catch.
哦，这是一个很棒的粉丝抓包。

621
00:28:26.840 --> 00:28:28.360
I promise I didn't write it.
我向你们保证，这不是我写的。

622
00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:31.560
We shot this episode about two weeks after the Emmys,
我们拍摄这集是在艾美奖颁奖典礼大约两周后，

623
00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:37.000
and I guess someone had written up on the board a little congratulations to us,
我想有人在白板上写了对我们的简短祝贺，

624
00:28:37.020 --> 00:28:41.600
and we also needed to say that Steve was robbed because he did not win that year for Michael Scott.
而且我们也需要表达史蒂夫被坑了，因为他那一年没有凭迈克尔·斯科特获奖。

625
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:43.600
He never won for Michael Scott.
他从来没有凭迈克尔·斯科特得过奖。

626
00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:45.200
Which is ridiculous.
这简直荒谬。

627
00:28:45.680 --> 00:28:45.880
Yeah.
对啊。

628
00:28:45.880 --> 00:28:52.940
Well, I have a Jenna catch, because since Celeste turned me on to looking at this whiteboard,
好吧，我有个詹娜抓包，因为自从塞莱斯特启发我去留意这块白板后，

629
00:28:53.160 --> 00:28:55.000
I found something else on the whiteboard.
我在白板上又发现了别的东西。

630
00:28:55.320 --> 00:29:00.300
On the top line written under Thursday, written in multiple colors, it says,
在星期四下方的那行置顶字是用多种颜色的笔写的，上面写着：

631
00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:03.920
In case you haven't noticed, there is a lot of colorful hooey on this board.
如果你还没注意到的话，这块白板上其实有很多五颜六色的废话。

632
00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:10.060
Anyway, guys, for the future, I think it could be very fun to freeze on this whiteboard,
总之，各位，以后我觉得暂停看这块白板会非常有意思，

633
00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:12.320
because they did change what they wrote all the time.
因为他们一直在更改上面写的内容。

634
00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:13.300
Well, I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

635
00:29:13.300 --> 00:29:20.360
I love the little subtle shade towards the television academy about Steve not getting the Emmy.
我喜欢这种对电视艺术与科学学院关于史蒂夫没拿到艾美奖的暗讽。

636
00:29:21.180 --> 00:29:21.420
Totally.
完全同意。

637
00:29:21.760 --> 00:29:25.760
Coming up next, Michael has a talking head, and then he does something immediately after,
接下来，迈克尔有一段单独访谈，然后他紧接着做了一件事，

638
00:29:25.940 --> 00:29:29.300
and it's one of these classic Michael moments that I live for.
这是我最期待的迈克尔经典时刻之一。

639
00:29:29.420 --> 00:29:30.860
It always makes me laugh so hard.
每次都把我笑得前仰后合。

640
00:29:31.300 --> 00:29:36.600
Michael says that all he can do is put on a brave face and be our leader,
迈克尔说他唯一能做的就是强颜欢笑，当我们的领导，

641
00:29:36.600 --> 00:29:39.460
and then he says to the whole bullpen,
然后他对整个大办公室的人说：

642
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:40.620
It's over!
结束了！

643
00:29:40.620 --> 00:29:42.060
We are screwed!
我们完蛋了！

644
00:29:42.480 --> 00:29:42.820
Yeah.
对啊。

645
00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:44.320
Like, really, buddy?
就这？真的吗，老兄？

646
00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:46.420
That's the brave face you're putting on for us?
这就是你为我们摆出的坚强表情？

647
00:29:46.520 --> 00:29:47.260
Okay, thanks.
好吧，谢谢。

648
00:29:47.520 --> 00:29:50.800
Yeah, I mean, he really, he offers no comfort.
对，我是说，他真的，他根本提供不了一点安慰。

649
00:29:51.140 --> 00:29:53.180
He sort of begins to ugly cry.
他开始有点丑态毕露地大哭起来。

650
00:29:53.680 --> 00:29:57.260
Angela is asking about the employees, asking about their jobs.
安吉拉在打听员工的情况，询问他们的工作。

651
00:29:57.500 --> 00:29:59.160
I have two catches here.
我这里有两个发现。

652
00:29:59.280 --> 00:30:01.340
I have something I need to say, Angela.
我有些话必须得说，安吉拉。

653
00:30:01.620 --> 00:30:02.120
Okay, go.
好的，说吧。

654
00:30:02.420 --> 00:30:05.940
At 7 minutes 18 seconds, your sweater?
在7分18秒的时候，你的毛衣？

655
00:30:05.940 --> 00:30:07.440
It's a sweater veSt.
那是件毛衣背心。

656
00:30:07.780 --> 00:30:08.180
It's a sweater veSt.
那是件毛衣背心。

657
00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:13.600
Okay, so I actually have some photos of this sweater from a wardrobe fitting that I saved.
好吧，其实我保留了一些这件毛衣在试装时的照片。

658
00:30:14.460 --> 00:30:20.640
So I have a button-down shirt, and then over it, I have a sweater vest, but it's like a tank.
所以我穿了一件纽扣衬衫，外面套了一件毛衣背心，但它就像是一件背心。

659
00:30:20.640 --> 00:30:26.760
It's like a teeny, tiny, very odd sweater veSt.
它就像是一件极小、极短、非常古怪的毛衣背心。

660
00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:32.420
It's like another one of those failed project runway contests.
它就像是《天桥骄子》里那种设计失败的参赛作品。

661
00:30:32.420 --> 00:30:33.920
Oh, 100%.
噢，百分之百是。

662
00:30:33.920 --> 00:30:42.440
And then our wardrobe designer, Carrie Bennett, took the buttons off the sweater vest and replaced them with those cat faces.
然后我们的服装设计师凯莉·贝内特取下了毛衣背心上的纽扣，换成了那些猫咪脸。

663
00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:44.060
It's really a work of art.
这真是一件艺术品。

664
00:30:44.200 --> 00:30:45.220
It really is.
确实如此。

665
00:30:45.220 --> 00:30:46.780
All right, well, I have a catch.
好吧，我有了一个发现。

666
00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:52.680
At 7 minutes 27 seconds, this is one of the most famous Michael Scott memes.
在7分27秒的时候，这是迈克尔·斯科特最著名的表情包之一。

667
00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:59.240
It's Steve making that face, like he's about to cry, or maybe he smells dog poop.
就是史蒂夫做出那个表情，好像他快要哭了，或者可能是闻到了狗屎味。

668
00:30:59.380 --> 00:30:59.860
You know the face.
你知道那个表情。

669
00:30:59.920 --> 00:31:02.180
And he says, this is the worSt.
他说，这是最糟糕的。

670
00:31:02.200 --> 00:31:05.340
And people use it a ton to respond to other people.
人们经常用它来回复别人。

671
00:31:05.460 --> 00:31:08.000
Like when they get some news that they're like, no way.
比如当他们听到某些消息时觉得，不会吧。

672
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:11.940
All of a sudden, I see in my feed Steve's face.
突然之间，我在动态里看到了史蒂夫的脸。

673
00:31:11.940 --> 00:31:18.180
Okay, on Office Ladies Pod, will you please post the pictures of your cat buttons and of this meme?
好的，在“办公室女士”播客上，你们能发一下你的猫咪纽扣和这个表情包的照片吗？

674
00:31:18.660 --> 00:31:20.420
Yes, of course, of course.
可以，当然可以。

675
00:31:20.620 --> 00:31:23.080
Okay, good, because I want everyone to have these visuals.
太好了，因为我想让每个人都看到这些画面。

676
00:31:23.860 --> 00:31:25.460
Okay, I think it's important.
好的，我觉得这很重要。

677
00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:29.200
I have a script question, Jenna, because I know you have the scripts.
我有关于剧本的问题，珍娜，因为我知道你有剧本。

678
00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:34.260
So, Toby admits that he knows that this was going to happen.
托比承认他知道会发生这种事。

679
00:31:34.420 --> 00:31:36.980
Michael calls him a traitor, says he wants to see him in his office.
迈克尔骂他是叛徒，说要他在办公室见他。

680
00:31:37.380 --> 00:31:41.820
They start to walk in, and Michael says, oh, my God, you walk so slowly.
他们开始走进去，迈克尔说，天哪，你走得太慢了。

681
00:31:41.940 --> 00:31:43.740
I feel like that was Steve improvising.
我觉得那是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

682
00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:46.500
I had that same feeling, and I did look at the script.
我也有同感，而且我确实查了剧本。

683
00:31:46.880 --> 00:31:51.360
None of that part of him calling Toby into his office was scripted.
他叫托比去他办公室的那部分全都没有写在剧本里。

684
00:31:52.700 --> 00:31:57.240
So, him, that whole bit of him calling Toby in his office, say he's walking slowly,
所以，他叫托比去办公室、说他走得很慢的整段戏，

685
00:31:57.260 --> 00:32:02.320
and then Dwight guarding the door and putting his hand up to the camera, none of that was in the script.
还有德怀特守在门前把手挡在摄像机前，这些都不是剧本里有的。

686
00:32:03.120 --> 00:32:03.560
Amazing.
太棒了。

687
00:32:04.180 --> 00:32:04.440
Yeah.
是的。

688
00:32:04.620 --> 00:32:04.920
Amazing.
太棒了。

689
00:32:05.160 --> 00:32:06.700
And I love that everyone just went with it.
我喜欢每个人都顺着演下去了。

690
00:32:06.860 --> 00:32:09.040
They just were like, oh, Steve's doing his thing.
他们只是觉得，噢，史蒂夫在自由发挥了。

691
00:32:09.200 --> 00:32:11.240
We're going to let this play out and participate.
我们要让它演下去并参与进来。

692
00:32:11.940 --> 00:32:12.460
Because I looked.
因为我查过了。

693
00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:16.380
I was like, wait, is there a lost scene of Toby in Michael's office?
我在想，等等，是不是有一场托比在迈克尔办公室被删掉的戏？

694
00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:18.860
Is there a conversation that didn't make it?
是不是有一段没播出的对话？

695
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:19.340
No.
没有。

696
00:32:19.560 --> 00:32:22.220
No, that was just Steve on the day.
没有，那只是史蒂夫当场发挥的。

697
00:32:22.600 --> 00:32:22.840
Wow.
哇。

698
00:32:23.040 --> 00:32:27.380
And, you know, speaking of how Rain gets the little smirk when he improvises,
而且，你知道的，说到雷恩在即兴发挥时怎么会露出那种假笑，

699
00:32:27.660 --> 00:32:33.420
at 7 minutes 52 seconds, when he won't let the camera crew in and he shuts the door,
在7分52秒的时候，当他不让摄影组进去并关上门时，

700
00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:35.000
he has the smirk.
他露出了那种假笑。

701
00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:36.280
I noticed it, too.
我也注意到了。

702
00:32:36.460 --> 00:32:36.760
Uh-huh.
嗯。

703
00:32:37.720 --> 00:32:42.680
Well, we had a fan question from Mary Poulton, and actually a lot of people wrote in with a similar
我们收到了玛丽·普尔顿的一个粉丝提问，其实很多人都写信问了类似

704
00:32:42.680 --> 00:32:43.200
question.
的问题。

705
00:32:44.120 --> 00:32:50.320
She wanted to know, when we got the script for this episode, did any of us worry that
她想知道，当我们拿到这一集的剧本时，大家有没有担心过

706
00:32:50.320 --> 00:32:52.520
the show was being canceled?
这节目要被砍了？

707
00:32:52.740 --> 00:32:55.920
Or did we know that this was just an idea for an episode?
还是说我们早就知道这只是剧集的一个构思？

708
00:32:56.820 --> 00:33:00.860
And she was asking, and a lot of people were asking, because we've said before, sometimes
她这么问，也有很多人这么问，是因为我们以前说过，有时候

709
00:33:01.320 --> 00:33:04.340
plots are revealed to us at these table reads, and they were shocking.
剧情是在剧本围读时才向我们揭晓的，而且往往很震撼。

710
00:33:04.640 --> 00:33:08.620
And they wanted to know, as we sat down and got the script, as we were reading it, were
他们想知道，当我们坐下来拿到剧本、开始阅读时，

711
00:33:08.620 --> 00:33:10.400
we thinking, wait a second, what?
会不会在想，等一下，什么？

712
00:33:10.560 --> 00:33:11.260
Scranton's closing.
斯克兰顿要关门了。

713
00:33:11.360 --> 00:33:12.220
Are we all out of jobs?
我们是不是都失业了？

714
00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:13.380
No, guys.
不，各位。

715
00:33:13.380 --> 00:33:15.400
We knew that this was a plot point.
我们知道这只是一个剧情转折点。

716
00:33:15.900 --> 00:33:17.820
None of us were worried.
我们谁都没有担心。

717
00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:21.560
We had all had our contracts renewed for all of season three.
我们的第三季合约全都已经续签了。

718
00:33:21.820 --> 00:33:22.120
Yeah.
对。

719
00:33:22.720 --> 00:33:26.740
And so we knew that we would be producing 24 episodes in season three.
所以我们知道我们在第三季会制作24集。

720
00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:31.660
And we also had been tipped off to the fact that eventually there would be a merger episode
而且我们还提前得到了风声，知道最终会有一个合并集，

721
00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:34.500
and that those people from Stanford would be coming to join us.
斯坦福的人会来加入我们。

722
00:33:34.580 --> 00:33:38.480
So we didn't have any kind of surprise or anxiety when we got this script.
所以当我们拿到这个剧本时，没有任何惊慌或焦虑。

723
00:33:38.480 --> 00:33:43.640
No, we were just excited because it meant finally, after this episode, we could all be in one
没有，我们只有兴奋，因为这意味着终于在这集之后，大家可以聚在

724
00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:44.200
room together.
同一个房间里了。

725
00:33:44.400 --> 00:33:45.520
So we were excited.
所以我们很兴奋。

726
00:33:45.660 --> 00:33:47.640
At least the Scranton branch, we were excited.
至少斯克兰顿分公司，我们很兴奋。

727
00:33:47.780 --> 00:33:48.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

728
00:33:48.320 --> 00:33:52.460
Maybe Stanford was like, we like our schedule, but we were excited to have everyone back.
也许斯坦福会觉得，我们挺喜欢自己的时间表的，但我们很高兴大家能聚在一起。

729
00:33:52.740 --> 00:33:53.220
All right.
好的。

730
00:33:53.340 --> 00:33:58.880
So now, Angela, we move into Orion talking head, and he's holding up his business cards,
那么现在，安吉拉，镜头转到了奥斯卡的单采，他手里拿着名片，

731
00:33:59.020 --> 00:33:59.180
right?
对吧？

732
00:33:59.260 --> 00:34:01.060
Or are they his calling cards?
或者那是他的私人名片？

733
00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:02.400
Oh, boy.
天哪。

734
00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:06.780
He's holding up his business slash calling cards.
他拿的是商务兼私人名片。

735
00:34:07.460 --> 00:34:08.620
Eight minutes.
八分钟。

736
00:34:09.180 --> 00:34:13.640
Notice, here it is, talking head exterior window behind him.
注意，就是这里，单采，他身后是外景窗。

737
00:34:14.040 --> 00:34:15.620
Oh, nice.
哦，不错。

738
00:34:15.620 --> 00:34:20.360
This is the beginning of the exterior window talking heads because next up, Angela has a
这是外景窗单采的开始，因为接下来，安吉拉有一个

739
00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:25.920
talking head and Kelly has a talking head with the mascara on her face, all exterior windows.
单采，凯莉脸上带着睫毛膏也有一个单采，全都是外景窗。

740
00:34:26.200 --> 00:34:27.680
She's going to track it.
她要记录下来。

741
00:34:27.980 --> 00:34:28.400
All right.
好的。

742
00:34:28.480 --> 00:34:32.580
So now we're going back to Stanford, and Andy is leading everyone in a chant.
现在我们要回到斯坦福，安迪正带头喊口号。

743
00:34:32.780 --> 00:34:33.940
Stanford, Connecticut.
康涅狄格州斯坦福。

744
00:34:35.340 --> 00:34:35.940
Right?
对吧？

745
00:34:35.940 --> 00:34:37.300
He's getting everyone worked up.
他在调动大家的积极性。

746
00:34:37.640 --> 00:34:44.100
So while everyone's chanting, at eight minutes, 23 seconds, you will see someone who is beloved
所以在大家喊口号的时候，在八分二十三秒，你会看到一个深受

747
00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:45.960
by our office cast and crew.
我们办公室剧组和演员喜爱的人。

748
00:34:46.080 --> 00:34:47.100
Her name is Lori Sox.
她叫洛瑞·索克斯。

749
00:34:47.240 --> 00:34:48.480
She was our stand-in.
她是我们的替身演员。

750
00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:52.400
Her and her husband, Stephen, they were like a stand-in duo team.
她和她的丈夫斯蒂芬，他们就像是一对替身黄金搭档。

751
00:34:52.560 --> 00:34:54.560
And she's in the background in the scene.
而且她在那个场景的背景里出现.

752
00:34:54.680 --> 00:34:56.460
And it just made me so happy to see her.
看到她真的让我感到非常高兴.

753
00:34:56.740 --> 00:34:57.900
I saw her, too.
我也看到她了.

754
00:34:58.120 --> 00:34:58.920
I saw her, too.
我也看到她了.

755
00:34:59.000 --> 00:34:59.740
And I loved it.
而且我超喜欢.

756
00:34:59.880 --> 00:35:03.020
Well, maybe we should explain what a stand-in is if we haven't before.
好吧，如果我们之前没解释过的话，也许我们该解释一下什么是替身.

757
00:35:03.020 --> 00:35:09.480
So after you rehearse a scene with the actors, you bring in people to stand in for the actors
所以在演员彩排完一场戏后，你会找人来代替演员站位

758
00:35:09.480 --> 00:35:12.580
while the crew sets the lights and the camera angles.
